<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
Maps physical Monarch controls to Android keycodes so they reach onKeyDown.
None of these keycodes are auto-forwarded, so each needs its own entry here
or it never arrives.

- Enter: not a chassis button. It is Dot 8 on the braille keyboard. Without
  this entry KEYCODE_ENTER (66) never reaches onKeyDown. This is the pause
  trigger (LiveGraphActivity.togglePause()).

Zoom In/Out are reserved by the device's screen reader for braille line
spacing and cannot be overridden by any mapping here. The Live/Overview
toggle uses D-pad Up/Down instead (see LiveGraphActivity).

D-pad center and Space are deliberately not mapped. The D-pad has no center
push on this device, and Space is a modifier prefix for reserved shortcuts,
so mapping it bare risks colliding with them.

PlantWaveApplication hands this file to KeySoft on launch.
-->
<keymapping>
    <application package="org.aph.plantwave">
        <context viewIdResourceName="SelfBraillingWidget">
            <action name="substitute">
                <command commandId="enter" param="66">
                    <key>Dots8</key>
                </command>
            </action>
        </context>
    </application>
</keymapping>
